    "frames": [
      {
        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "A lilac transmission glass lung with a frosted pink airway tree and ringed trachea. A thin periwinkle acrylic scan slab with engraved lines and a glowing scan line crosses it at the lower lobes. One gold bead sits in the overlap on the right lobe and throws a warm streak along the scan line. Plum studio sweep, with a contact shadow under the slab and lobes.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline, a scan plane covers only part of the lung and catches a second, unexpected gold object where it crosses the glass. The bead is the one warm point in the frame and reads as 'found'. The section ring on the slab shows exactly where the cut meets the lobe.",
        "weakness": "Minor. At native size the bronchial tips end in thin spiky claws rather than rounded tips (tile r2c1, design x 640 to 920, y 520 to 640). The lower lobes under the slab go muddy olive and brown where the glass meets the plum shade (tiles r3c1 and r3c2, design y 900 to 1200). That is a dirty tone against the vivid palette. Neither breaks the subject. The glass, rim, slab edge, bead and cast all read as finished materials.",
        "repair": "none required",
        "encoding_reads": true,
        "dominant_subject_finished": true,
        "feed_legible": true,
