      {
        "slide": 9,
        "role": "close",
        "subject": "The cover's glass lung restaged unflagged on a warm apricot-coral sweep at right, seen lower and from the other side. It has a continuous rounded airway tree and ringed trachea. Each lobe is crossed by three bevelled scan slabs at shoulder, mid chest and base, each with a glowing scan line and a periwinkle section edge. A plum contact shadow sits under the bases.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline, scans at any height all touch the lung and none of them holds a bead. The glass between the slabs stays clear. The cover's object returns as the reader's own unanswered scan, which sets up 'ask what yours showed'.",
        "weakness": "Minor. The slabs read as pale pink-white discs with a thin periwinkle outline more than as periwinkle acrylic, so the deck's colour code for 'scan for something else' is weaker here than on frames 1 and 6. At native size the right lobe's base slab has a small kink in its front rim and outline (tile r3c2, design x 540 to 580, y 1080 to 1100). Neither defect breaks the subject. The glass, rims, airway and contact shadow are finished, and the lung reads clearly at feed size.",
